kosha hardness

  -- resistance to permanent deformation (scratching, indentation).
  -- Mohs scale: 1 (talc) to 10 (diamond).
  -- diamond: sp3 covalent bonds in all directions — no planes of weakness.
  -- graphite: same atoms, layered structure — very soft.
  -- hardness ≠ toughness: glass is hard (7 Mohs) but brittle.

